From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:37:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: mixer: Add the A733 mixer

The A733 display engine uses the DE33 layout: its layers, top and
display windows, the blender and the VI channel registers sit at the
offsets of the H616 mixer.

Add a configuration with one VI channel as primary plane, RGB only
with the channel colour space converter at 0x800 of the channel window
kept off, and the VI scaler of that channel. Further planes need the
blender input mux in the top block, which is not supported. No module
clock rate is forced: the user manual advises against retuning PLL_DE,
which also clocks the interconnect, so DE0 runs at the PLL_DE rate the
boot chain set up. The vendor kernel sets 600 MHz.

Not covered: UI channels, more VI channels, YUV formats, the register
command queue.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the mixer scanned out
the framebuffer, and the frame CRC reported by the sink changed with
each colour written to it.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
index b6cd7352e76c..3c7682bd09c5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
@@ -879,6 +879,29 @@ static const struct sun8i_mixer_cfg sun50i_h616_mixer0_cfg = {
 	.map		= {0, 6, 7, 8},
 };
 
+/*
+ * The A733 display engine follows the DE33 register layout. Only VI
+ * channel 0 is described: the blender input mux that a second plane
+ * needs is not supported. The channel colour space converter sits at
+ * 0x800 of each channel window; its coefficient layout is not supported,
+ * so it is written off and the layer takes RGB only. The module clock
+ * rate is not set: the user manual advises against changing PLL_DE,
+ * which also clocks the interconnect (section 4.1.4.3), so DE0 runs at
+ * the PLL_DE rate the boot chain set up. The vendor kernel sets 600 MHz.
+ */
+static const struct sun8i_mixer_cfg sun60i_a733_mixer0_cfg = {
+	.lay_cfg = {
+		.ccsc		= CCSC_DE33_CHANNEL_LAYOUT,
+		.de_type	= SUN8I_MIXER_DE33,
+		.scaler_mask	= 0x1,
+		.rgb_only	= 1,
+	},
+	.de_type	= SUN8I_MIXER_DE33,
+	.ui_num		= 0,
+	.vi_num		= 1,
+	.map		= {0},
+};
+
 static const struct of_device_id sun8i_mixer_of_table[] = {
 	{
 		.compatible = "allwinner,sun8i-a83t-de2-mixer-0",
@@ -928,6 +951,10 @@ static const struct of_device_id sun8i_mixer_of_table[] = {
 		.compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-de33-mixer-0",
 		.data = &sun50i_h616_mixer0_cfg,
 	},
+	{
+		.compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-de-mixer-0",
+		.data = &sun60i_a733_mixer0_cfg,
+	},
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, sun8i_mixer_of_table);
